        "original_id": "de983a10-62c9-5d0e-a434-ca9cce3c395a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Herz, Lloyd Kaufman, Roland Emmerich\n- Companies: Troma Entertainment, Centropolis Entertainment\n- Films: The Noah's Ark Principle, Sgt. Kabukiman N.Y.P.D., The Toxic Avenger series, Tromeo and Juliet\n- Topics: independent film studios, comedic horror films\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Roland Emmerich directed The Noah's Ark Principle as part of his university thesis work in the film industry.\n- In 1985, Roland Emmerich and his sister co-founded Centropolis Entertainment.\n- Michael Herz and Lloyd Kaufman are the co-founders of Troma Entertainment.\n- Troma Entertainment is described as the world's longest-running independent film studio.\n- Troma Entertainment is known for comedic horror films including The Toxic Avenger series and Tromeo and Juliet.\n- Sgt. Kabukiman N.Y.P.D. is a 1990 superhero comedy film directed by Lloyd Kaufman and Michael Herz.\n- Troma Entertainment distributed Sgt. Kabukiman N.Y.P.D..",
